  "description": "A gravel bike? A 90’s mountain bike? Who cares? This bike is unconcerned with labels. It’s a proportionally sized titanium ATB(all terrain bike) built for loaded up long hauls, serendipitous mid-commute singletrack sessions, and whatever else you think you shouldn’t be doing on a 700c bike.\n\nWith room for up to 700c x 2.0″ (50 mm) tires and our ONERIDE proportional sizing, the Puritan blends gravel efficiency with comfort and stability. Load it up with bags to get lost in the woods, or pedal it to the pub. We don’t make the rules.\n\nThe Puritan is purpose-built to run a flat bar and a 60mm stem. Yes, you can build it with drop bars, but it will stretch out the rider triangle. Sorry, not sorry. This bike is unapologetically flat-bar first.\n\nA gravel bike? A 90’s mountain bike? Who cares? This bike is unconcerned with labels. It’s a proportionally sized titanium ATB(all terrain bike) built for loaded up long hauls, serendipitous mid-commute singletrack sessions, and whatever else you think you shouldn’t be doing on a 700c bike.\n\nWith room for up to 700c x 2.0″ (50 mm) tires and our ONERIDE proportional sizing, the Puritan blends gravel efficiency with comfort and stability. Load it up with bags to get lost in the woods, or pedal it to the pub. We don’t make the rules.\n\nThe Puritan is purpose-built to run a flat bar and a 60mm stem. Yes, you can build it with drop bars, but it will stretch out the rider triangle. Sorry, not sorry. This bike is unapologetically flat-bar first.",
